   "id": "bava_batra.20b.7",
   "daf": "20b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "וְאֶת הַתַּנּוּר – שְׁלֹשָׁה מִן הַכִּלְיָא, שֶׁהֵן אַרְבָּעָה מִן הַשָּׂפָה. אָמַר אַבָּיֵי: שְׁמַע מִינַּהּ, כִּלְיָא דְּתַנּוּר טֶפַח; נָפְקָא מִינַּהּ לְמִקָּח וּמִמְכָּר.",
   "en": "The mishna teaches: «And» there must be a distance of «three» handbreadths «from the» protruding «base» of «an oven» until the wall, «which is four» handbreadths «from the» narrow «upper rim» of the oven. «Abaye said: Learn from» the mishna that «the base of an oven» is «a handbreadth» wider than its rim. The practical «difference» of this observation is with respect «to buying and selling,» i.e., a buyer should know that this is the proper ratio for the dimensions of an oven."
  }
